2025-08-01 17:21:42,315 - config.config - INFO - Command: python3 src/f5_tts/infer/infer_cli.py --gen_text Okay, welcome back to database marketing. This week, we will review some of the important statistical concepts that we need to keep in mind while we progress through this course. . We will start with the basics of probability, . which is the foundation of all statistical analysis. . Without a good understanding of probability, . it's hard to make sense of any statistical data. . So, let's start with the basics. . What is probability? . Probability is the measure of the likelihood of an event occurring. . It's a number between 0 and 1, . where 0 means the event will never happen, . and 1 means the event will always happen. . But, in reality, . most events fall somewhere in between. . So, let's take a look at some examples. . For instance, . what's the probability of rolling a 6 on a fair six-sided die? . Well, . there's only one way to roll a 6, . and six ways to roll any other number. . So, the probability of rolling a 6 is 1 out of 6, . or 1/6. . Now, . let's talk about some statistical concepts that are related to probability. . One of these concepts is the normal distribution. . The normal distribution is a probability distribution that is symmetric about the mean, . which means that the mean, . the median, . and the mode are all equal. . The normal distribution is also known as the bell curve, . because it looks like a bell when plotted on a graph. . The normal distribution is very important in statistics, . because it's used to model many types of data, . such as heights, . weights, . and IQ scores. . Another statistical concept that's related to probability is the concept of independence. . Independence is a property of events, . where the occurrence of one event does not affect the probability of another event. . For example, . if you flip a coin, . the probability of getting heads is 1/2, . regardless of whether you got tails or heads on the previous flip. . Finally, . let's talk about some statistical concepts that are related to both probability and independence. . One of these concepts is the concept of conditional probability. . Conditional probability is the probability of an event occurring, . given that another event has occurred. . For example, . if you roll a die, . the probability of rolling a 6 is 1/6, . but if you roll a 6, . the probability of rolling a 6 again is 1/6, . because the two events are independent. . So, . that's a review of some of the important statistical concepts that we need to keep in mind while we progress through this course. . --ref_audio /tmp/tmpf5y9w3cr_ref.wav --ref_text /tmp/tmpqyh_ml_f_ref.txt --output_dir /tmp --output_file tmp3243tmgt_clone.wav --speed 0.8 --nfe_step 32 --cross_fade_duration 0.2
